course: dictionary
lesson: 7840
title: Racist: words about unfair treatment
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Racist is an adjective. It describes words, actions or ideas that treat people unfairly or badly because of their race, skin colour or where their family comes from. Racist can also be a noun: a racist is a person who believes some races are better than others, or who treats people unfairly because of race.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «If someone makes a racist or mean joke, do not laugh; say it is not okay or tell an adult.» The words not okay and tell an adult show that a racist joke is wrong. Ask yourself: what does the sentence tell me to do? Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
explain: «Racism is treating people badly because of their race or where their family comes from.» Racist bullying is teasing or being unkind to someone for these reasons, and it should always be reported to a teacher or another adult. Standing with the person being bullied is part of being fair.
fact: Racist describes words, actions or ideas that treat people unfairly because of race, skin colour or family background.
fact: A racist is a person who believes some races are better than others, or who treats people unfairly because of race.
fact: «A racist comment» and «racist bullying» are wrong and should be reported to a teacher.
fact: Anti-racist means standing against racism and unfair treatment.
fact: In history lessons, pupils learn about racist laws and about people who fought against them, such as Martin Luther King Jr and Rosa Parks.
exercise: «If someone makes a racist joke, what should you do?» | Laugh along so they feel included | Repeat the joke to your friends | *Say it is not okay or tell an adult | Make a joke back
exercise: What does racist describe? | Weather that is grey and wet | *Words, actions or ideas that treat people unfairly because of race | Food that is very spicy | Music that is very loud
exercise: «Anti-racist» means what? | Living by the sea | Liking every kind of music | *Standing against racism and unfair treatment | Running very fast
test: «Racist bullying should always be what?» | Copied | Forgotten | *Reported to a teacher or adult | Ignored
test: Which of these is a racist? | Someone who reads a book about history | Someone who lives in a big city | *Someone who believes some races are better than others | A person who has a pet cat
exam: Why is a racist joke wrong? | It is too long to remember | It is written in a book | It is funny to everyone | *It treats people unfairly because of their race
